    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0235" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/294: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-13T12:00:00-06:00">July 13,
                        1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>263. I have just had a talk with Minister Suarez<anchor n="51" xml:id="d290-f1"/>
                    who heads the delegation to Habana. He will leave next Thursday. He tells me
                    that President Cardenas has given him instructions, which accord with his <pb
                        facs="0236" n="224" xml:id="pg224"/> own feelings, to cooperate fully with
                    the delegation from the United States in the carrying out of plans for
                    continental solidarity. He says, “Our Government sees eye to eye with the United
                    States.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d290-f1" n="51" xml:id="d290-f1-content">
                <p>Eduardo Suarez, Minister of Finance and Credit, personal representative of the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
